body:

# What are Masterclasses?
PyCon DE Masterclasses are hands-on, full-day workshops led by experienced trainers. Participants buy a separate ticket for each Masterclass and spend the day diving deep into one topic together with an expert.

The Masterclasses take place on Monday, 19 April 2027 in Heidelberg, the day before the conference opens. Each Masterclass runs from 9:00 to 16:00, with a one-hour lunch break at 12:00. Groups are small: 8–20 participants.

## What participants get

 * A high-quality training session
 * Unique insights from an expert
 * Hands-on experience
 * The opportunity to network with other participants and with the trainers

## What trainers get

 * A speaker ticket for the conference
 * Reimbursement of travel and accommodation costs within Europe (€800 against receipts, per Masterclass)
 * A chance to promote your expertise and services
 * The freedom to hand out as much merch as you like
 * Visibility as a contributor to the conference
 * The opportunity to discuss your plan with a member of the Masterclass Committee
 * Feedback from participants after your Masterclass

## How do I submit a proposal?

Please fill in the [form](https://forms.gle/VTaych5YaAALmYJh9)
The form asks you to describe and structure your training in some detail. We believe that doing this early leads to a better training and a better experience for our community.

## What to bear in mind

We believe that an excellent way to provide a high-quality experience — and to have fun doing so — is to team up with another trainer. Give it a thought.
We expect Masterclasses to provide direct value to participants, so we discourage topics that mainly advertise a product.

If you are interested in running a sponsored Masterclass, [please contact sponsoring](/sponsoring).

We expect to publish the first wave of Masterclasses end of October 2026.

## How are proposals selected?
Masterclasses are handpicked by a committee. We pay attention to the trainers' expertise and training methodology, and we do our best to select a balanced mix of interesting topics. There is no deadline, we will select suitable Masterclasses as they fly in.
